// run
// #5429: a `decimal` as an ANONYMOUS-tuple member panicked `gpSizeOpc: width
// 16`, through a different mechanism from #5417/#5420/#5427's enum-payload
// fix: `buildTupleIn`'s write (compiler/lowerexpr.bit) typed the FieldSet off
// the raw `decimal` member type (16 bytes) while the value it stored was the
// two-word `decimalTupleType` tuple every decimal VALUE is (8-byte pointer).
// `tupleElem`'s read had the identical mismatch. A named class field's
// decimal member was already correct (#3982's own `emitDecimalFieldSet`
// path) — this is specific to the boxed anonymous-tuple/closure-env shape.
fn pair(): (decimal, int) {
  return (3.5, 7)
}

fn main() {
  let (d, n) = pair()
  println("${d} ${n}")
}
